<title>USA: CORESTAFF sees margins pressured.</title>
<headline>CORESTAFF sees margins pressured.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>CORESTAFF Inc said maintaining margins for its Information Technology staff augmentation services will be challenging because of rising consultant costs and as users pressure their vendors to hold the line on costs.</p>
<p>CORESTAFF said pro forma gross margin for the current quarter was 50 basis points below that for 1996.</p>
<p>A significant portion of the company's first quarter growth came from large customers and these accounts typically have lower gross margins, but higher operating leverage, CORESTAFF said.</p>
</text>
